{{also|blech}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|}}, from {{inh|de|goh|bleh}}; ultimately from the same root as {{m|de|bleich}}. Compare {{cog|osx|blek}}, {{cog|nl|blik}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/blɛç/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Blech.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɛç}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n||gen2=Bleches|Bleche}}

# [[sheet]] (of metal)
# {{lb|de|informal|music}} [[brass|Brass]], a collective term for all brass instruments, or all brass players, etc.
#: {{ux|de|„Das '''Blech''' spielt bitte mal alleine!“ rief der Dirigent.|The conductor demanded loudly: “Brass play on their own now, please!”}}

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-n|(e)s|e}}

